{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1349066-unified-tier-2-character-creation","id":1349066,"title":"Unified Tier 2 Character Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-17T07:13:08-08:00","id":1349066,"title":"Unified Tier 2 Character Creation","content":"Essentially this works for all character types. First, build the mundane baseline including one extra Attribute point and the four Edges. After that you get 55 XP to spend on the character and you buy everything. A Nova spends 16 XP for Quantum 1. An Inspired spends 10 XP for the first point of Inspiration. Psions/Psiads buy at least two point of Psi for 24 points. However, Psions do receive one extra Attribute point due to the Promethues Chamber. <br /> <br /> I might edit this after looking more closely at Superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:19:43-08:00","id":1349211,"title":"","content":"I still haven't looked in-depth at Superiors yet, but I do have a couple of notes. Under this concept it is completely possible to build a really skilled but otherwise mundane person. In truth such a person could be terrifyingly effective in a mixed group. While Psis, Novas and Talents are directly powerful, they have to (or at least most likely will) spend much of their XP at the start and over time on Gifts/Powers/Modes/Psi/etc. The mundane character, on the other hand, can focus purely on skills and edges. While those eventually kind of max out, there's nothing that says a person who starts mundane has to stay that way. A highly capable mundane could potentially erupt as a Nova, develop latent psionics or be Inspired to becomes a Talent.<br /> <br /> Tier II Novas reflect either Novas who came about prior to 2018 or those rare Novas who erupt in the Aeon era without completely losing their humanity, the ones who defied the quantum storm and clung to what made them people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:30:23-08:00","id":1350459,"title":"","content":"And... I think I'm scrapping this idea for the most part. The XP thing rapidly devolved into stocking up on skills. Unless I've missed something huge, at character creation you get a total of 9 dots to allocate to your skills based on your Paths. It's bizarre to me that the character one would think would be somewhat beyond skills is the one best positioned to acquire them: the nova.<br /> <br /> So, for Tier II Novas, after the paths and Attributes are distributed, they get 75 XP, 1 point of Quantum, 1 Att point for their Favored Approach and must select Fame or Alt. Identity in the Nova era. In Trinity they may get either a free level of either Alt ID or Dormancy. They can also take the Attribute point or an additional Tainted point of Quantum plus Dormancy 1. For every point of Quantum they get at least 1 point of Transcendence. If they get to Quantum 4 they'll have at least 5 point of Transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 11-23-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T17:03:39-08:00","id":1351166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1349066-unified-tier-2-character-creation#post1349066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially this works for all character types. First, build the mundane baseline including one extra Attribute point and the four Edges. After that you get 55 XP to spend on the character and you buy everything. A Nova spends 16 XP for Quantum 1. An Inspired spends 10 XP for the first point of Inspiration. Psions/Psiads buy at least two point of Psi for 24 points. However, Psions do receive one extra Attribute point due to the Promethues Chamber.<br /> <br /> I might edit this after looking more closely at Superiors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did something similiar in my character creation process <a href=\"https://www.worldanvil.com/w/creation/a/landing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It's about half way down the page. I'm converting Vampire the Requiem to Storypath, with and eye on how Chronicles of Darkness handled templates for supernaturals.<br /> <br /> best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 11-26-2019, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}